4. Zipping and Unzipping
Compress the test_dir directory into a file named test_dir.zip using zip.
Unzip test_dir.zip into a new directory named unzipped_dir.
=============
Answer ->
  #zip -r test_dir.zip test_dir 
  #unzip test_dir.zip -d /home/ubuntu/unzipped_dir

One thing to remember that by default in Ubuntu destro, zip and unzip are not available in the system, we need to install those by using below commands - 
  #sudo apt install zip
  #sudo apt install unzip

Also there are two commands which can be used for the similar purpose, those are tar and untar. 
Example -> tar -cvf <archive file name>.tar.gz <target folder/file name>
           tar -xvf <archive file name>.tar.gz

Here -c stands for compress and -x stands for extract. 
