7. Working with Environment Variables
Use export to set a new environment variable called MY_VAR with the value "Hello, Linux!".
=============
Answer ->
  #export MY_VAR="Hello, Linux!"

Export basically assign some value to a variable or in other words, environment variable. 
Now if we assign any value to a variable and then call it using echo command and a doller sign infront of the variable, we should see the actually value in the temrinal which was assigned to it. 
